      "writtenOn": "2026-05-29T17:37:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The only use of the document parameter is for the names of the mark params which are interned. I wrote a test to check cross-document behavior but because of the way the test harness is set up it\u0027s not easy to keep two documents live in memory at the same time. I believe it would work cross document as long as you keep the memory around for the original since the only reference is the interned strings. That would cause a copy of the mark to be emitted when the PDF text is generated.\n\nI added to the documentation about this since I don\u0027t have a nice way to make it work. Maybe that can be future work to clean up this strings memory ownership and then cross document marks would work without a caveat.\n\nHere\u0027s that test I wrote:\n\n```\n--- a/fpdfsdk/fpdf_edit_embeddertest.cpp\n+++ b/fpdfsdk/fpdf_edit_embeddertest.cpp\n@@ -4150,6 +4150,50 @@ TEST_F(FPDFEditEmbedderTest, AddExistingMarkCompressedStream) {\n   CheckMarkCounts(saved_page.get(), 0, 2, 2, 0, 0, 0);\n }\n \n+TEST_F(FPDFEditEmbedderTest, AddExistingMarkCrossDocument) {\n+  ASSERT_TRUE(OpenDocument(\"hello_world.pdf\"));\n+  ScopedPage page \u003d LoadScopedPage(0);\n+  ASSERT_TRUE(page);\n+\n+  // Add a mark to the first page object\n+  FPDF_PAGEOBJECT page_object1 \u003d FPDFPage_GetObject(page.get(), 0);\n+  FPDF_PAGEOBJECTMARK mark \u003d FPDFPageObj_AddMark(page_object1, \"Prime\");\n+  EXPECT_TRUE(mark);\n+  EXPECT_TRUE(FPDFPageObjMark_SetStringParam(document(), page_object1, mark,\n+                                             \"Test\", \"Hello\"));\n+\n+  // Render and check there is 1 mark.\n+  {\n+    ScopedFPDFBitmap page_bitmap \u003d RenderPage(page.get());\n+    CompareBitmapWithExpectationSuffix(page_bitmap.get(), kHelloWorldPng);\n+  }\n+  CheckMarkCounts(page.get(), 0, 2, 1, 0, 0, 0);\n+\n+  // Open another document\n+  auto document \u003d std::move(document_);\n+  CloseDocument();\n+  ASSERT_TRUE(OpenDocument(\"hello_world_compressed_stream.pdf\"));\n+  page \u003d LoadScopedPage(0);\n+  ASSERT_TRUE(page);\n+\n+  // Render and check there are no marks.\n+  {\n+    ScopedFPDFBitmap page_bitmap \u003d RenderPage(page.get());\n+    CompareBitmapWithExpectationSuffix(page_bitmap.get(), kHelloWorldPng);\n+  }\n+  CheckMarkCounts(page.get(), 0, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0);\n+\n+  // AddExistingMark with the mark created for the other document\n+  FPDF_PAGEOBJECT page_object2 \u003d FPDFPage_GetObject(page.get(), 0);\n+  EXPECT_TRUE(FPDFPageObj_AddExistingMark(page_object2, mark));\n+\n+  {\n+    ScopedFPDFBitmap page_bitmap \u003d RenderPage(page.get());\n+    CompareBitmapWithExpectationSuffix(page_bitmap.get(), kHelloWorldPng);\n+  }\n+  CheckMarkCounts(page.get(), 0, 2, 1, 0, 0, 0);\n+}\n+\n TEST_F(FPDFEditEmbedderTest, SetMarkParam) {\n   // Load document with some text.\n   ASSERT_TRUE(OpenDocument(\"text_in_page_marked.pdf\"));\n```",
